From the 022 console runs (handoff of 2026-11-10). Two compute rejections repeated on every dispatch:
- 6f9367bd41dc0b58 +0x340, TLD4.F16 with per-tap offsets (bits 76-78 = 2): lowered like the 32-bit
  per-pixel gather (coordinates the pair at A, offsets the pair at B) with the FP16 packing.
- 9387db798781f081 +0x4b50, LEA.HI with bit 63: -Rb, as the plain 0x211 form already reads bit 63;
  Maxwell IADD negate-B (bit 48). Bit 62 is still rejected.
FP16 packing put c0 in the high half in the gather and one more path (Eglantine dc3e912fb7 fixed the
TEX path the same way). Per-tap offsets that are not constants were dropped in SPIR-V; one gather
per tap now (ported from Eglantine 993a31c593, from Duck912 1e02498099). Rejections are logged per
shader/instruction/reason at the 1st, 2nd, 4th... time; handle-zero lines are no longer capped at
32 and say where the handle program stopped. EDEN_NX2_NO_HANDLE_ZERO turns handle 0 off. Bumps the
translator salt.

